<section class="ref-group"><h2>Battles <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-guandu"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-guandu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Guandu</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 200</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Guandu was fought in 200 CE near the Yellow River in northern China between the warlords Cao Cao and Yuan Shao.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-white-wolf-mountain"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-white-wolf-mountain.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of White Wolf Mountain</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 207</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of White Wolf Mountain was fought in 207 in present-day Liaoning between the forces of the Chinese warlord Cao Cao and the Wuhuan, who were sheltering Yuan…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-red-cliffs"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-red-cliffs.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Red Cliffs</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 208</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Red Cliffs was fought on the Yangtze in the winter of 208–209, at the end of the Han dynasty.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-xiaoting"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-xiaoting.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Xiaoting</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 221–222</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Xiaoting, also called the Battle of Yiling, was fought in 221–222 in western Hubei, China, between Liu Bei of Shu Han and Sun Quan's Eastern Wu.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hormozdgan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-hormozdgan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Hormozdgan</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 224 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Hormozdgan was fought in 224 CE between Ardashir I and the Parthian king Artabanus IV.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-wuzhang-plains"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-wuzhang-plains.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Wuzhang Plains</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 234</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Wuzhang Plains was a stand-off in 234 between the Shu Han army of Zhuge Liang and the Wei forces of Sima Yi, on the Wei river in modern Shaanxi, China.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-edessa"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-edessa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Edessa</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 260 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Edessa was fought in 260 CE in upper Mesopotamia between the Roman emperor Valerian and the Sasanian king Shapur I.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-immae"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-immae.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Immae</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 272</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Immae was fought in 272 near Antioch in Syria between the Roman emperor Aurelian and the army of the Palmyrene Empire under Zabdas.</span></a></li></ul></section>
